  "articleBody": "Ever walk into your kitchen and just feel… cramped? It's a common complaint, especially in older homes or layouts that just don't fit modern living. A small kitchen isn't just an inconvenience; it can truly limit how you use your home, from meal prep to entertaining. Sometimes, it's about a lack of counter space or storage, making everyday tasks a puzzle. Other times, the layout itself feels like a maze, cutting off flow to other rooms. We see this often in Las Vegas homes where kitchens were designed for a different era.\n\nOne big reason for a ",
